IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-81, TARGETED: the Land Law, 5729-1969 ("the Law"; the English title is a working translation, not an enacted title). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records four references and amending instructions that touch the Law (items I1 to I4) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the reader of the Law who follows one of the four references to the instrument the reference names. A row of references asks that reader no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument as its footer prints it, a reference in the Law, a table of section numbers and its rows, a section as a page prints it, an instruction that prints a status word, three kinds of instruction on section 72(a) (put a string in after a string; put a string in the place of a string; rename a law), a commencement clause, a provision of another law that the row did not read, a provision of the Interpretation Law as printed, and the questions asked of them. No reference is stated here; they are in ll81-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Each item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is missing, says something else, or has a status word printed for it, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
--
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. NotChecked is a value, not an absence: it marks a provision the row names and did not read.
-- An instrument is typed as Printed: the row says what a page prints and when its issue is dated, and nothing about any other status.
-- Hebrew is typed in code only where the very same words are on a quotation line in ll81-cross-references.l4 or in the deposited excerpt (tools/hebcheck.py checks that).

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `The status of an instrument as the row types it` IS ONE OF
    Printed

DECLARE `A status in the instruments read` IS ONE OF
    NotChecked

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page images`
    `official page images; that no later instrument touched the citing words rests only on the consolidation's untagged heading line (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
    `official page images; the list of the instruments after the first one that prints an instruction on the section rests on the consolidation's tag list (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`

-- An instrument as its footer prints it. `the issue date its footer prints` is the date of the issue, never a day of effect; where no page read prints a date it is NOTHING.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its citation` IS A STRING
    `its title as a deposited page prints it` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the issue date its footer prints` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `its status as the row types it` IS A `The status of an instrument as the row types it`
    `the printed pages deposited` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- A reference in the Law, or the words of an instruction that cites a provision: the place where it is printed, the words, and the name and number it gives.
DECLARE `A reference in the Law` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the place in the Law` IS A STRING
    `the instrument that prints it` IS A `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the citing words` IS A STRING
    `the name or title the citing words give` IS A STRING
    `the number the citing words give` IS A STRING
    `the subsection the citing words give` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- One row of a table of section numbers, as printed: the cell under the heading for the new section and the cell under the heading for the previous section. A cell is a string because a cell can print more than a number.
DECLARE `A row of a table of section numbers` HAS
    `the new-section cell` IS A STRING
    `the previous-section cell` IS A STRING
    `the block it is printed in` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A table of section numbers` HAS
    `the instrument that prints it` IS A `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the sub-heading of the block that opens it` IS A STRING
    `the title inside that sub-heading` IS A STRING
    `the heading of the new-section column` IS A STRING
    `the heading of the previous-section column` IS A STRING
    `the rows the row types` IS A LIST OF `A row of a table of section numbers`

-- A section as a page prints it: its number, its margin note, a mark printed beneath the margin note, and the words of an entry the row types.
DECLARE `A section as a page prints it` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its number as printed` IS A STRING
    `its margin note` IS A STRING
    `the mark printed beneath the margin note` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the defined words of an entry the row types` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the words after the dash of that entry` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- An instruction that prints a status word for a provision of another instrument (item I3).
DECLARE `An instruction that prints a status word for a provision` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the place in the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note` IS A STRING
    `the number it names` IS A STRING
    `the title tail it names` IS A STRING
    `the status word it prints` IS A STRING
    `the commencement the pages read print` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the label of the next subsection` IS A STRING
    `the next subsection as a string, not evaluated` IS A STRING

-- Three kinds of instruction on section 72(a) of the Law (item I4).
DECLARE `An instruction that puts a string in after a string` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the place in the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note` IS A STRING
    `the string it puts the new string after` IS A STRING
    `the string it puts in` IS A STRING
    `the commencement the pages read print` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `An instruction that puts a string in the place of a string` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the place in the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note` IS A STRING
    `the string it replaces` IS A STRING
    `the string it puts in the place` IS A STRING
    `the commencement the pages read print` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `An instruction that renames a law` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the place in the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note` IS A STRING
    `the title before the instruction` IS A STRING
    `the title after the instruction` IS A STRING
    `the commencement the pages read print` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- A commencement clause as printed: the numbers of sections it names, and the day each paragraph prints, if any.
DECLARE `A commencement clause as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the place in the instrument` IS A STRING
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note` IS A STRING
    `the section numbers it names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the day paragraph (a) prints` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day paragraph (b) prints` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- A provision of another law that the row names and did not read.
DECLARE `A provision of another law` HAS
    `the law it belongs to` IS A STRING
    `its number as printed` IS A STRING
    `its status in the instruments read` IS A `A status in the instruments read`
    `where the row names it` IS A STRING

-- A provision of the Interpretation Law as printed (applies to all four items): its words as one string and as a list of words split on spaces.
DECLARE `A provision of the Interpretation Law as printed` HAS
    `its section number` IS A NUMBER
    `its margin note` IS A STRING
    `the instrument that prints it` IS A `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its words as one string` IS A STRING
    `its words split on spaces` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `An item of the row` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words` IS A `A reference in the Law`
    `the tags the consolidation's heading line of the section carries` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

-- A table, as a lookup. The new-section cell printed against a previous-section cell, if the table prints that previous cell in one of the rows the row types.
GIVEN p IS A STRING, rs IS A LIST OF `A row of a table of section numbers`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF r's `the previous-section cell` EQUALS p
        THEN JUST (r's `the new-section cell`)
        ELSE `the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` p rest

GIVEN n IS A STRING, rs IS A LIST OF `A row of a table of section numbers`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the previous-section cell printed against the new cell` MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF r's `the new-section cell` EQUALS n
        THEN JUST (r's `the previous-section cell`)
        ELSE `the previous-section cell printed against the new cell` n rest

GIVEN n IS A STRING, rs IS A LIST OF `A row of a table of section numbers`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of rows that print the new cell` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the new-section cell` EQUALS n) rs)

GIVEN p IS A STRING, rs IS A LIST OF `A row of a table of section numbers`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of rows that print the previous cell` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the previous-section cell` EQUALS p) rs)

-- Items I1 and I2, the question the red assertion asks: is the number the citing words give the new-section cell the table prints against that number as a previous-section cell?
GIVEN c IS A `A reference in the Law`, t IS A `A table of section numbers`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the number cited is the new-section cell the table prints against it` MEANS
    (JUST (c's `the number the citing words give`)) EQUALS (`the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` (c's `the number the citing words give`) (t's `the rows the row types`))

-- The same test, applied to a row read from the table and not to a reference: the previous cell p is printed against the new cell n.
GIVEN t IS A `A table of section numbers`, n IS A STRING, p IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the table prints the new cell against the previous cell` MEANS
    (`the new-section cell printed against the previous cell` p (t's `the rows the row types`)) EQUALS (JUST n)

-- The title the citing words give is the title inside the sub-heading of the table.
GIVEN c IS A `A reference in the Law`, t IS A `A table of section numbers`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the title in the citing words is the title in the table's sub-heading` MEANS
    c's `the name or title the citing words give` EQUALS t's `the title inside that sub-heading`

-- Item I3, the question the red assertion asks: does an instruction in the list print the status word for the number and the title tail the citing words name?
GIVEN c IS A `A reference in the Law`, w IS A STRING, i IS A `An instruction that prints a status word for a provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction prints the status word for the cited provision` MEANS
    ((i's `the number it names`) EQUALS (c's `the number the citing words give`))
    AND ((i's `the title tail it names`) EQUALS (c's `the name or title the citing words give`))
    AND ((i's `the status word it prints`) EQUALS w)

GIVEN c IS A `A reference in the Law`, w IS A STRING, ins IS A LIST OF `An instruction that prints a status word for a provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no instruction in the list prints the status word for the cited provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER ins
        WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
        WHEN i FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (NOT (`the instruction prints the status word for the cited provision` c w i)) AND (`no instruction in the list prints the status word for the cited provision` c w rest)

-- Item I4. Words and strings.
GIVEN w IS A STRING, ts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of times the word occurs among the words` MEANS count (filter (GIVEN t YIELD t EQUALS w) ts)

GIVEN ts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the words joined with single spaces` MEANS
    CONSIDER ts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN ""
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN foldl (GIVEN acc, t YIELD CONCAT acc, " ", t) x rest

-- One row of a table, built from its three printed parts.
GIVEN n IS A STRING, p IS A STRING, b IS A STRING
GIVETH A `A row of a table of section numbers`
`a row of a table as printed` MEANS
    `A row of a table of section numbers` WITH
        `the new-section cell` IS n
        `the previous-section cell` IS p
        `the block it is printed in` IS b

-- A step applied by hand: the clause before the step is the part before, the string the instruction replaces, and the part after; the clause after the step is the part before, the string the instruction puts in the place, and the part after.
GIVEN b IS A STRING, r IS A STRING, a IS A STRING, clause IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the clause is the part before, the string, and the part after` MEANS
    clause EQUALS (CONCAT b, r, a)

-- Limb (a) of I4, the question the red assertion asks.
GIVEN c IS A `A reference in the Law`, ri IS A `An instruction that renames a law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the short title in the citing words is the title printed after the instruction` MEANS
    c's `the name or title the citing words give` EQUALS ri's `the title after the instruction`

GIVEN c IS A `A reference in the Law`, ri IS A `An instruction that renames a law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the short title in the citing words is the title printed before the instruction` MEANS
    c's `the name or title the citing words give` EQUALS ri's `the title before the instruction`

-- Limb (b) of I4: an instruction names a string when the string occurs in the words it replaces or in the words it puts in.
GIVEN i IS A `An instruction that puts a string in the place of a string`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the replacing instruction names the string` MEANS
    (CONTAINS (i's `the string it replaces`) w) OR (CONTAINS (i's `the string it puts in the place`) w)

GIVEN i IS A `An instruction that puts a string in after a string`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the inserting instruction names the string` MEANS
    (CONTAINS (i's `the string it puts the new string after`) w) OR (CONTAINS (i's `the string it puts in`) w)

-- A section number is one of the section numbers a commencement clause names.
GIVEN k IS A `A commencement clause as printed`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the clause names the section number` MEANS elem n (k's `the section numbers it names`)

-- The date order of two instruments' issue dates, when both are printed.
GIVEN a IS A `An instrument`, b IS A `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first instrument was issued before the second` MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `the issue date its footer prints`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST da THEN
        CONSIDER b's `the issue date its footer prints`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST db THEN da < db

-- Whether the title the deposited page prints for an instrument contains a string.
GIVEN a IS A `An instrument`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the title of the instrument contains the string` MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `its title as a deposited page prints it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST t THEN CONTAINS t w
